hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1104","Chapter on supplication at the time of fighting, 1143 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub informed us, he said: Abu Hazim ibn Dinar informed me, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two supplications are not rejected - or he said: are never rejected - supplication at the call to prayer and at the moment of battle when men join one another in combat."
